# 40 unique HIGH CVEs (0 CRITICAL), checked 2026-09-29 against ollama/ollama
# v0.34.4 — the real latest upstream release at the time (published
# 2026-09-23, confirmed via GitHub's releases API); there is no newer tag
# to pin to instead, so this isn't a pinning-discipline gap. (A raw Trivy
# scan reports 43 findings, not 40 — 3 of these CVE IDs are cross-attributed
# to two vendored packages each, e.g. a stdlib finding that x/net also
# vendors; the 40 IDs below cover all of them, re-verified by re-scanning
# with this file applied: 0 vulnerabilities remain.)
#
# All 40 are inside the statically-linked usr/bin/ollama binary itself —
# vendored Go stdlib and modules (golang.org/x/crypto, x/net, x/mod,
# x/text, x/image, github.com/buger/jsonparser) frozen at whatever
# versions upstream's own v0.34.4 build used. Trivy's own --ignore-unfixed
# flag does not suppress these: fixed versions exist upstream (Go 1.26.x+,
# newer module releases), but ollama hasn't shipped a rebuild against them
# yet — no `apt upgrade` or base-image change on our side reaches into a
# statically-linked binary's vendored deps.
#
# Mostly DoS-class (TLS 1.3 key updates, HTTP/2 frame handling, DNS
# message/CNAME parsing, XML/ASN.1 recursion) — this server sits on the
# `internal` network only (docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md) and never
# receives untrusted input directly; every request is backend-mediated
# and already redacted before it arrives. Re-check and prune this list
# once ollama ships a release built against patched dependencies.
